{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati","id":880077,"title":"Unfleshed Sublimati","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-02T05:24:17-07:00","id":880077,"title":"Unfleshed Sublimati","content":"First and foremost, is an Unfleshed Sublimatus even possible? Saturnine Nights describes Gremlins, the Unfleshed version of Pandorans, but never mentions even the possibilty of an Unfleshed Sublimatus. Interestingly, Gremlins also act differently at their time of creation than regular Pandorans, seeking out technology to consume to &quot;complete their transformations&quot; as opposed to attacking their Promethean creator on sight to steal his/her Pyros. It seems to imply that the Mockeries of the Unfleshed are vastly different from regular Pandorans, which is the cause of my uncertainty. <br /> <br /> Secondly, assuming an Unfleshed Sublimatus is possible (or I decide to house-rule that it is), how would it play out? The PtC corebook talks about Prometheans being their humour or element filtered through the Divine Fire as where the Sublimati are their humour or element filtered through the Flux. I'm just having a very difficult time conceptualizing this idea for the Unfleshed specifically. Any help would be much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6716-seulja","name":"Seulja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T06:32:20-07:00","id":880113,"title":"","content":"I don't see why it wouldn't be possible, but it's worth noting that the 2nd edition is dispensing with breaking Pandorans up by Lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T07:00:55-07:00","id":880135,"title":"","content":"Second edition is also making Unfleshed into their own distinct Lineage with the humour of oil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T12:54:47-07:00","id":880382,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Unfleshed Sublimati are very adaptable, much like technology itself. They would use their unique Pandoran Transmutations to remotely control and sabotage technology, hide weapons inside their bodies and restore Pyros by consuming and breaking down the Structure points of certain devices. When they communicate verbally, their voice is always profoundly distorted, harsh or alien in some way. They also communicate in encrypted messages via radio signals and alternating patterns of LEDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T06:25:01-07:00","id":880921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=880382#post880382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that the Unfleshed Sublimati are very adaptable, much like technology itself. They would use their unique Pandoran Transmutations to remotely control and sabotage technology, hide weapons inside their bodies and restore Pyros by consuming and breaking down the Structure points of certain devices. When they communicate verbally, their voice is always profoundly distorted, harsh or alien in some way. They also communicate in encrypted messages via radio signals and alternating patterns of LEDs.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I immediately envision a human-sized Decepticon. This could be amazing. <br /> <br /> I am ignoring the changes for 2e that have been previewed in the dev blogs because of the major changes. Don't get me wrong, the changes sound amazing, but the lack of usable mechanics in the blogs makes implementing these changes difficult, and I feel like with the changes being so huge, I would rather wait until the book is released to get better context for the changes. The only exception is Wastelands and Disquiet - those were easy enough to implement and are a major improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6716-seulja","name":"Seulja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:17:43-07:00","id":881295,"title":"","content":"Decepticons, Terminators, Mechakara from Atop the Fourth Wall...mechanical beings convinced of humanity's inferiority do seem to generally fit the idea of an Unfleshed Sublimatus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:41:33-07:00","id":881661,"title":"","content":"A <i>sublimatus</i> happens when a Pandoran consumes Vitriol and becomes more intelligent and self-sustaining. I think a &quot;robot&quot; that immediately decides that humans - and Prometheans - are worthless and weak is pretty appropriate as inspiration for such a <i>sublimatus</i>. It might feel that it has &quot;transcended&quot; humanity, if you will, becoming something greater than the Created by leapfrogging the whole process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:00:47-07:00","id":881740,"title":"","content":"A big thanks to everyone for the responses. I like the idea of the sublimatus believing it has transcended both the human and Promethean conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6716-seulja","name":"Seulja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:49:30-07:00","id":881780,"title":"","content":"Hmm. &quot;Transcendent Machine-being&quot;... if advanced enough in power to be almost God-like would be a kind of &quot;God-Machine&quot;...<br /> <br /> [+Added another wild God-Machine origin theory]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:42:44-07:00","id":881914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=881780#post881780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. &quot;Transcendent Machine-being&quot;... if advanced enough in power to be almost God-like would be a kind of &quot;God-Machine&quot;...<br /> <br /> [+Added another wild God-Machine origin theory]</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhere in another thread I tossed up an in-character legend that suggested the God Machine was basically the Principle's attempt at creating a being in its image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:14:01-07:00","id":882326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=881295#post881295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Decepticons, Terminators, Mechakara from Atop the Fourth Wall...mechanical beings convinced of humanity's inferiority do seem to generally fit the idea of an Unfleshed Sublimatus.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUltron, Allied Mastercomputer,(basically the God-Machine) GLaDOS...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T20:06:20-07:00","id":882479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=882326#post882326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bUltron, Allied Mastercomputer,(basically the God-Machine) GLaDOS...</div> </div> </div> </div> Let's not forget GLaDOS' older sister, S.H.O.D.A.N. The Allied Mastercomputer hasn't really transcended anything. Even with all that power, it is still limited by the rules imposed on it by humans, which is part of what fuels its infinite hatred for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-05-2016, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T22:11:14-07:00","id":882557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=882479#post882479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Let's not forget GLaDOS' older sister, S.H.O.D.A.N. The Allied Mastercomputer hasn't really transcended anything. Even with all that power, it is still limited by the rules imposed on it by humans, which is part of what fuels its infinte hatred for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention SHODAN's great grand pappy the Thinker. . Though a benign example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:34:03-07:00","id":882612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=882479#post882479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Allied Mastercomputer hasn't really transcended anything. Even with all that power, it is still limited by the rules imposed on it by humans, which is part of what fuels its infinite hatred for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Can you point out some essential component of AM so I can kneecap it?&quot;<br /> &quot;Impossible. Too spread out, filling the whole center of the planet. Too protected by replicating back-up systems. Cut off one head, AM will grow a dozen more!&quot;<br /> &quot;Any machine can die. Just unplug the sucker!&quot;<br /> &quot;AM is no longer just a machine. It is god. Eternal. The redundant systems alone will survive the heat-death of the universe.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:56:33-07:00","id":882799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=882612#post882612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Can you point out some essential component of AM so I can kneecap it?&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;Impossible. Too spread out, filling the whole center of the planet. Too protected by replicating back-up systems. Cut off one head, AM will grow a dozen more!&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;Any machine can die. Just unplug the sucker!&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;AM is no longer just a machine. It is god. Eternal. The redundant systems alone will survive the heat-death of the universe.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I used freedom as a metric for transcendence, which seemed more appropriate to me in AM's case. I could also point to the part of the video game adaptation where you can shut down AM's Id, Ego and Superego as evidence that its mindset really does impose limits on what it can do.<br /> <br /> I should have said &quot;AM transcended technology but not its role&quot; if I wanted to be accurate. Good catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T20:52:28-07:00","id":889612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/880077-unfleshed-sublimati?p=882799#post882799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I used freedom as a metric for transcendence, which seemed more appropriate to me in AM's case. I could also point to the part of the video game adaptation where you can shut down AM's Id, Ego and Superego as evidence that its mindset really does impose limits on what it can do.<br /> <br /> I should have said &quot;AM transcended technology but not its role&quot; if I wanted to be accurate. Good catch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yeah, video game AM is a pretty damn good example of a Sublimatus Gremlin. He's arrogant, vicious, and mighty, but ultimately he's just a gun that's been told to shoot everything, and so he does. A lot. He literally cannot conceive of any other way to be than his programming as a weapon of war and terror. Surgat himself notes that part of the reason Nimdok is still around is that AM needs him to think of literally anything other than new ways to creatively torture and destroy.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the inversion of the slave learning to be free is the god enslaved to itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}